# Compendium packs.
#
# A compiled pack is a live LevelDB, and Foundry writes to it whenever it opens one:
# CURRENT is rewritten and a fresh MANIFEST-* is spawned on open, and the .ldb files are
# rewritten on compaction. Committing that means every pull collides with whatever the
# local Foundry did last, which is exactly what happened. Ignoring only the churn is not
# an option either — CURRENT and MANIFEST-* are what make the store readable at all.
#
# So packs/_source is the committed form and the LevelDB is a build artefact:
# run 
> alternity-v2@1.0.0 build:packs
> node tools/build-packs.mjs

alternity-achievements    190 documents -> packs/alternity-achievements
alternity-armor            94 documents -> packs/alternity-armor
alternity-cybertech        58 documents -> packs/alternity-cybertech
alternity-equipment       226 documents -> packs/alternity-equipment
alternity-fx              234 documents -> packs/alternity-fx
alternity-skills          214 documents -> packs/alternity-skills
alternity-species          22 documents -> packs/alternity-species
alternity-templates        59 documents -> packs/alternity-templates
alternity-weapons         258 documents -> packs/alternity-weapons after cloning, and after any pull that touched packs/_source.
packs/*
!packs/_source
